      "content": "Expanding on management styles, the \"drag\" often comes from high expense ratios in actively managed mutual funds, where professional management fees compound and can significantly outperform passive ETFs that mimic market indices. While mutual funds charge a larger upfront management fee, ETFs typically have fee structures that are transparent and often lower, reducing long-term erosion of returns. It is crucial for your client to calculate the post-fee performance of each option, as lower fees directly translate to higher net returns regardless of market conditions. Including these cost comparisons in your memo will highlight the direct financial impact of choosing between active and passive strategies.",
